[center][size=6][b]Remnant 2 Save Editor[/b][/size]
[size=3]Analyze and edit your Remnant 2 saves — resources, items, archetypes, teleport, world stones, Blood Moon, world loot.[/size]
[size=2]Free & open source · English / Русский · v1.5.0[/size][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]⚠ Read first[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Close the game completely[/b] (not just to the main menu) before saving. The editor refuses to save while Remnant 2 is running.
[*]Every save makes an automatic [b]backup[/b]; the [b]Backups…[/b] window restores any of them.
[*]Unofficial fan tool, use it in [b]solo play[/b] and at your own risk.
[*]Tested with the [b]Steam[/b] version on Windows. Epic is untested. [b]Xbox / Game Pass saves are not supported.[/b]
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Character[/b] — archetype XP (one-click max level), power level, trait rank and trait points.
[*][b]Resources[/b] — Scrap, Lumenite, Relic Dust, irons, Blood Moon Essence, DLC alloys…
[*][b]Inventory[/b] — quantities and upgrade levels, capped at the game's maximum ([b]+10 for boss / special weapons[/b], +20 standard, 10 mutators). Delete rings, amulets, armor, mutators, consumables and materials (refuses anything equipped, attached or bound to the radial menu).
[*][b]Quest items[/b] — see the quest items each world keeps (keys, coins…); duplicate Crimson King Coins.
[*][b]Traits[/b] — trait levels with a live budget: warns before you overspend.
[*][b]Add item[/b] — catalog of ~700 rings, amulets, armor, relics, engrams, mutators, consumables and materials, with "where to get it in game".
[*][b]Teleport[/b] — choose where you spawn on the next load: world stones (with their in-game names) and checkpoints.
[*][b]Open world stones[/b] — make one or all world stones of a world available in the in-game travel menu.
[*][b]Blood Moon[/b] — make the game roll a Blood Moon on the next zone load.
[*][b]World analysis[/b] — bosses, dungeons, events and pickups of your current roll, their loot and what you already own. Handy for checking a reroll without walking the map (works while the game is running — just don't save).
[*][b]All fields[/b] — raw editor for any value in [i]profile.sav[/i] / [i]save_N.sav[/i].
[*][b]Safety[/b] — undo (Ctrl+Z), list of changes, backup rotation, refuses to overwrite progress the game saved in the meantime, and opens a save [b]read-only[/b] if its format is not fully understood (e.g. after a game update).
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download the main file and unpack the [b]whole[/b] archive anywhere (e.g. your Documents).
[*]Run [b]Remnant2SaveEditor\Remnant2SaveEditor.exe[/b]. Keep it inside its folder next to [i]_internal[/i] — it doesn't start on its own. A desktop shortcut is fine.
[*]The editor finds your saves automatically ([i]%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\Remnant2\Steam\<id>[/i]); otherwise use [b]Open…[/b].
[/list]
No Python needed. Uninstall: delete the folder (settings live in [i]%APPDATA%\Remnant2SaveEditor[/i]).

Prefer to run from source? Everything is on [url=https://github.com/distrix11/Remnant2Editor]GitHub[/url] — [i]Start Editor.bat[/i] (needs Python 3.8+) or build the exe yourself with [i]build.bat[/i].

[line]

[size=4][b]What has been tested in game[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]✅ Resources (also creating missing ones), archetype XP, weapon upgrade levels.
[*]✅ Teleport to discovered world stones and to checkpoints (also in unexplored zones).
[*]✅ Opening all world stones of an adventure — travelling straight to the boss and killing him completed the story quest.
[*]✅ Duplicating Crimson King Coins — the Red Prince accepted the tribute and [i]Succession[/i] unlocked.
[*]✅ Summoning a Blood Moon.
[*]⚠ [b]Not checked in game yet:[/b] adding catalog items (same format as the tested resources), deleting items, trait levels, teleport to [b]undiscovered[/b] world stones (one test gave a black screen, another worked — the editor warns you).
[*]ℹ Items from a DLC you don't own stay locked in the inventory (same as DLC items received in co-op).
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Antivirus[/b][/size]
The exe is built with PyInstaller and is not code-signed — a common source of false positives. This release is the [b]folder build[/b]: in testing, Windows Defender did not flag it and VirusTotal showed one heuristic hit out of ~70. The exact same file is built automatically by GitHub Actions from the public source, so you can check what goes into it (or build it yourself).

[line]

[size=4][b]Bug reports[/b][/size]
Please use the [b]Bugs[/b] tab here or [url=https://github.com/distrix11/Remnant2Editor/issues]GitHub Issues[/url] and include:
[list]
[*]what you did and what happened;
[*]the log file [i]%APPDATA%\Remnant2SaveEditor\editor.log[/i];
[*]game version and platform (Steam / Epic).
[/list]
If a game update changes the save format, the editor opens your save read-only and tells you — nothing gets written. That is the moment to report it. This is a hobby project shared as is; I answer when I can.

